**Type call: 3w4, confidence high.** The tiebreaker is on the record — at eight years old she set a 6 a.m. alarm to do 500 crunches so she'd be in better shape than her brother. Unprompted, comparative, closed by labor. A Four would have made that difference into an identity; she just closed the gap.

**The thesis** inverts the standard read. The internet's verdict is "manufactured pop product." But the persona wasn't installed by a label — she built it herself at six because being in her own skin felt worse, and she later gave it a name (Tatiana) because *"I started to black out onstage and become this person that I couldn't explain, nor could my family or my friends, and I needed a reason for it."*

